    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
    <tr>
        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <p><b>Steps:</b></p>
<ul>
	<li>Go to the Gregory Olsen photo studio site (<a href="https://photostudio.demohoster.com/" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">https://photostudio.demohoster.com/</a>)</li>
	<li>Go to Work tab &gt; Lifestyle</li>
	<li>Navigate to page 3</li>
	<li>Click on any preview photo from this gallery.</li>
</ul>


<p><b>Actual result:</b> Clicking a photo should open a viewer that lets the user browse through all photos on that page</p>

<p><b>Expected result:</b> Clicking a photo opens only that single photo in a fixed/static view. There's no way to move to other photos.Need to manually use the browser's back button to exit and return to the gallery</p>
            <br/>
        </td>
    </tr>
    </table>

